WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.110
By "our next job," you mean when 
I went to deal with Jomatsu-san,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.420
and you were off somewhere else?

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:14.030
You just went to discuss the job, right?

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:14.740
Yeah.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.620
<i>Which means we're going to 
exorcise that yokai today?</i>

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.620
<i>I wonder what kind of yokai it is.</i>

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.320
I'm getting changed. Wait here.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.210
Okay.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:32.400
<i>Abeno-san seems more dispirited than usual.</i>

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:40.430
Hanae, what's our client like this time?

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.430
I haven't yet heard what kind 
of yokai hired us, either.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:44.440
Isn't this next job from 
a human and not a yokai?

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.330
Not a yokai, but a human?

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.150
I don't know anything 
else about it, though...

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.580
<i>They've been indirectly involved before,</i>

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:55.290
<i>but this is the first time a 
human has come directly to us.</i>

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:30.750
<b>Mystery 9 "The Marked Difference"</b>

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:27.750
Wow...

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:30.750
What a huge house.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.760
Welcome! Huh?

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.530
There's two of you today?

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.690
This is my assistant.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.300
My name's Ashiya. Nice to meet—

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.580
This way.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.830
Sorry we couldn't talk 
properly the other day.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:55.340
My mom suddenly came home.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:56.030
It's fine.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.280
<i>This girl is our client?</i>

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.490
The room we'd like you 
to exorcise is this way.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.130
It's my room.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.290
That's where the mysterious 
phenomena are happening?

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.750
That's right.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.290
<i>A room where mysterious things happen, huh?</i>

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.000
Um, what are these?

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.740
<i>This "forbidden room" 
couldn't be more obvious!</i>

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.200
They're sealing talismans I put up.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.750
I did some research online and 
stuck all kinds of them on.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.480
I don't think they worked, though.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:25.390
I see.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.300
I'm taking them off.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.310
But I worked so hard to put them up!

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.470
So that's it.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:36.480
Is there something in there?

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.370
There's a ghost?

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:39.400
What's it like? What kind of ghost?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.780
I was a little dubious,

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.600
but there's actually something in there.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.250
Abeno-san, what's inside?

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.850
Hairball, come.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.550
Um, what should I do?

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.790
Hey, what is it?

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.800
Make sure she doesn't come inside.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.500
What's in there?

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:55.500
Okay...

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.720
I want to watch you exorcise it! Let me see!

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.080
Hey, listen...

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.380
Could you move away from this room?

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.490
What? I won't get in the way.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:05.420
Let me watch.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.840
Well, you know, exorcisms require focus.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.900
Plus, it could be dangerous.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.870
Aww! I wanted to watch!

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:16.110
Are you enjoying this situation?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.190
Wh-What?

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.620
Ashiya-san, right?

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:22.730
Yes.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.290
What does an exorcism involve?

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.920
Well, it varies case by case...

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.760
Can you sense spirits, too?

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:31.790
You can, right?

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.370
After all, you're his assistant.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.510
Um...

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.890
You must have had scary experiences, right?

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.140
What's the scariest thing 
that's happened to you?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.050
I visit paranormal spots all the time.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.600
The one I went to the other day was...

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.680
E-Excuse me.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:46.590
What?

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.210
Exactly what kind of supernatural 
phenomena have been occurring?

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.460
Sometimes different parts 
of the room rattle and shake,

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.310
even though I'm not doing anything.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:58.200
It must be a poltergeist, right?

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.480
A polter...?

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.730
How long has it been happening?

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.740
Hasn't he told you anything?

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.240
Not really.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.980
He must not expect much from you.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.970
What do you think he's doing?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.750
Can I take a peek?

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.750
<i>Is this what human clients are like?</i>

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.790
<i>Maybe this is why Abeno-san 
seemed so depressed.</i>

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:24.480
<i>Anyway, I wonder what 
kind of yokai is inside.</i>

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.760
Who are you?

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:28.040
Mom, welcome home.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.880
He's an exorcist.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.100
H-Hello.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.430
<i>Is she glaring at me?</i>

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:37.550
<i>Did I do something rude?</i>

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:38.860
Unbelievable!

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:42.120
You actually went and hired one 
after I told you not to?

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.840
But I'm paying them with my own 
allowance, so what's the problem?

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.100
No one said you could waste your allowance!

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.400
I'm not wasting it!

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.070
They're real-life supernatural phenomena!

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:54.200
This is ridiculous!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.570
There's no such thing!

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:56.320
<i>Th-This isn't good.</i>

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.460
<i>If they make a scene now...</i>

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:57.600
There is too!

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.210
You're just imagining things!

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.910
I-In any case, please calm down.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:07.470
Well, there's no point in 
arguing about it out here.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.120
I'm having my daughter make some tea.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.110
Y-You didn't need to do that.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:24.700
<i>Are Abeno-san and Fuzzy okay?</i>

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:25.550
You...

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.740
Y-Yes?

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.240
You're a student, aren't you?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.150
I'm in my first year of high school.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:33.150
The boy in my daughter's room is the one

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:34.920
who came the other day, isn't he?

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:35.930
Is he a student, too?

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:39.270
Yes. We're classmates, technically.

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:45.260
Can you actually exorcise anything?

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.260
Honestly, I don't believe 
in this kind of thing.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.670
Right...

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.010
<i>I get it.</i>

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:53.720
<i>She's not glaring at me.</i>

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:56.010
<i>She just doubts us.</i>

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:59.530
I have trouble understanding
unscientific things.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:04.330
You do this because you believe 
you have a sixth sense, right?

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:06.830
S-Something like that.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:10.510
I can't exorcise anything, 
so I more or less assist him.

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:13.280
But you're familiar with the 
exorcising procedure, right?

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:16.540
<i>This conversation is starting 
to go in a bad direction.</i>

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:21.040
I'm sorry. I should go help him now.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.540
You're trying to run because you 
can't answer, aren't you?

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.080
That's not true at all.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.920
Then explain it to me.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.760
<i>Explaining it will be hard,</i>

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.050
<i>but I guess I just need to 
convey that we're doing a job.</i>

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.560
Well, you see, to exorcise something means...

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:47.950
I'll say it one more time!

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:50.730
Abeno-san opens portals to the Underworld

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:52.730
and sends yokai through them!

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:55.420
Only Abeno-san can open those portals!

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:58.200
People who can't see yokai 
can't see the portals, either!

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.790
What? Can't you explain it more scientifically?

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:02.580
<i>I'm screwed!</i>

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:06.380
<i>In any case, she didn't understand any 
of it, but I did explain it to her.</i>

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.760
<i>Besides, as long as the 
mysterious phenomena stop,</i>

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.480
<i>she shouldn't have an issue, right?</i>

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:12.090
<i>This time I'll run for it.</i>

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.920
Um, I really do need to go help him now.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.510
Is it all right if I go?

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:19.000
Fine, I understand.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:19.770
Then...

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.560
Listen, you.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.460
Don't you think you should quit this job?

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:35.700
Since I hired them, I should watch them work.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.860
What good is a job that you can't even explain?

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:46.300
Do your parents know what you're doing?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.750
I don't know your motivation for doing this job,

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:52.200
but if you don't want to be doing it,

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.880
I can introduce you to some proper jobs.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:00.080
Doing this kind of thing with that man

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.670
will take you off the right path.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:03.280
So—

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:03.850
Move.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.180
Do you get what I'm saying to you?

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:13.850
Abeno-san will exorcise the yokai

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:16.150
and make the mysterious phenomena stop.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:20.340
You can trust us.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.160
Seriously.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:25.290
An earthquake?

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:29.940
<i>Only this house is shaking.</i>

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:30.880
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:32.130
Hey!

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.880
Abeno-san!

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:41.800
You! What are you doing here?

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:45.060
Abeno-san!

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:47.550
What happened?

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.470
Where have you been?

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:52.570
Sorry. I got stuck talking to her mother.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.770
Hairball, do you know where it went?

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:01.880
It escaped?

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.870
Just when I nearly had him,

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.620
that girl opened the door.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:10.340
It stopped.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.920
Where is he, hairball?

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:15.440
Maybe he went outside.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.960
No, I can sense him.

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:20.280
He must be hiding somewhere inside the house.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.220
We'll have to search the entire building.

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:26.980
Excuse me.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.830
Wh-What's wrong with you?

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:32.410
Sorry. The yokai that was 
in your daughter's room

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:33.610
seems to have escaped.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:34.740
What?

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:37.490
We'll find it right away, so...

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:38.740
What?

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.260
What are you talking about?

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.490
A yokai? Are you serious?

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:47.990
<i>Even after my explanation, 
she still doubts us.</i>

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:49.240
Get out!

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.000
I've had enough of your games!

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.710
Games?

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.520
This is absurd! I can't stand this anymore!

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:58.130
Just leave already!

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.680
If you want us to leave that badly, we—

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:06.310
I apologize for the inconvenience 
our incompetence has caused you.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.590
We'll take care of it immediately.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:09.920
Abeno-san...

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:11.440
Did you not hear me?

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.790
I told you to leave.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:16.730
Where on earth did that girl go?

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:21.450
Fuzzy!

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:23.770
Again?

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.220
What is this?

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:27.390
I'm sorry,

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:31.240
but we must act to stop this immediately.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.580
Would it be all right if 
I checked the other rooms?

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:38.090
Just hurry up and do something 
about this! Quickly!

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:41.260
Hey, Fuzzy!

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.920
I-Is this...

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.260
Yeah, it is.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:55.730
<i>Since it was appearing in a girl's room,</i>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.980
<i>I assumed it was a cute little yokai.</i>

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:01.940
<i>Just what kind of yokai is this?</i>

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:07.990
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:11.380
Since we didn't find him on the first floor,

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.440
he must have fled to the second floor.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:15.790
If we're not careful, we'll lose him again.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:21.550
Hello? Is anyone there?

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:23.630
Hello?

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.750
Did something just...

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:33.850
Could it have been...

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:34.840
Don't go in there!

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:39.190
Hey, I felt something run past me just now.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.340
Could the amateurs

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.820
please refrain from getting involved?

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:57.160
Close the door.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.200
Okay.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:06.930
There he is.

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:10.520
Is that spiky thing the yokai?

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:13.430
He seems to have strayed into this house.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:15.140
He's shaking.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.780
He's extremely shy.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:21.190
Actually, it's more like he's terrified of humans.

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:23.800
Fuzzy was able to calm him down.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.860
I was just about to convince 
him to be exorcised, but...

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:34.730
This commotion seems to have 
frightened him even more.

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:38.240
I'm sorry for scaring you.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.860
It's all right now.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:41.460
Let's go to the Underworld.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:50.970
We'll have to wait until 
he calms down some more.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:03.660
<i>What good is a job that you can't even explain?</i>

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.220
Hey!

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:19.210
Ashiya!

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:21.250
Huh?

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:26.010
Hey, will you listen to what I have to say?

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:30.840
I was possessed by Fuzzy.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.690
It made me tired, dizzy, and nauseated.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.080
It was seriously scary.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.410
It was an awful time,

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.060
but now he's a dear friend to me.

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:44.900
Do you know why we became friends?

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.730
Because I happened to be able to see yokai?

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:52.760
No.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:55.850
It's because I learned that he possessed me

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:59.410
just because he was lonely.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.910
When I first saw him, I was really scared.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.070
But since then, I've met a lot of yokai.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:10.430
Now I'm not even scared to look at them.

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.430
Abeno-san and I are human,

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:17.430
but we understand that you're afraid.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:20.280
You don't know what to do

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:23.940
because you're not used 
to being around humans.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:40.960
The shaking...

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:43.430
Abeno-san.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.660
He seems to be okay now.

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:00.840
Look. They're best friends now.

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.850
Take care.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.360
Take care, Spiky.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:27.260
I'm sorry for the commotion we caused.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:28.380
It's fine.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:32.380
I'd like to return the fee that was paid to us.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:34.860
I don't care about the money.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:37.180
I still can't believe it.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:39.520
But since you actually 
seem to have helped us,

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:40.940
I should thank you.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:41.890
But...

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:44.770
Never come near my daughter again!

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:56.280
Huh?

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:09.670
I'm not mad at you. Just ignore me.

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:12.200
I'm not mad at you either, Fuzzy!

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.790
What was that woman's problem?

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:24.090
I understand why she doubted us,

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:26.650
but she didn't have to put it that way!

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:33.210
Listen. It's normal for people 
to talk to us that way.

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:35.200
This is normal?

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:36.700
Yeah.

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:40.140
They can't see them.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:43.950
They can't help their curiosity or doubts.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.420
<i>"They can't help it"? That's it?</i>

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:51.840
Abeno-san, you're awfully calm about this.

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:54.920
Do you always just ignore what they say?

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.720
I'm not calm at all.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.850
But giving heed to them is a pain in the ass.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.610
Huh? What's wrong?

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:15.760
Of course you're not fine.

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:17.100
Of course you're not.

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:18.300
<i>What now?</i>

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.520
They found it amusing and suspicious.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:23.180
They even said some nasty things about us.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:25.470
Of course nobody would enjoy that.

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:28.810
Nobody... And yet I said you seemed calm...

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:31.800
<i>He's the biggest pain of all today.</i>

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:34.150
Stand up, Ashiya.

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:42.100
I don't care anymore.

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:45.830
As long as I can exorcise 
yokai for the yokai's sake,

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:49.560
that's good enough for me.

00:18:55.890 --> 00:18:57.150
<i>For the yokai...</i>

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:00.700
<i>When the Legislator asked if I could</i>

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:04.390
<i>give my body and soul in service of yokai,</i>

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:06.950
<i>I couldn't say yes.</i>

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:11.610
<i>But Abeno-san is tasked with this job because</i>

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:13.670
<i>he's prepared to do that.</i>

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:16.670
<i>Though we're doing the same job,</i>

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:20.680
<i>in situations like these, 
whether or not we can accept it</i>

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:27.270
<i>is the definitive difference 
between me and Abeno-san.</i>

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:31.140
Here it comes, Fuzzy!

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:41.820
<i>I'm still not happy about 
what happened the other day.</i>

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:45.270
<i>But it doesn't bother me as much 
when I'm playing with Fuzzy.</i>

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.830
<i>Maybe this is what it feels 
like to be satisfied with</i>

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:54.380
<i>exorcising yokai for the yokai's sake.</i>

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:01.860
<i>You must be careful.</i>

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:05.380
<i>Ashiya-sama is dangerous.</i>

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.510
<i>He might be right.</i>

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:10.960
<i>Not because of his fear,</i>

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.600
<i>but because his feelings of 
attachment might grow stronger.</i>

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:18.730
Sorry, Fuzzy. Give me a minute.

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:21.240
Hello?

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.820
Yeah, I can talk.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:25.880
What's up, Zenko?

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:27.060
Abeno-san's here, too.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.250
We're still at school.

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:32.500
No, we don't have work.

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:34.700
Yeah. Uh-huh.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:38.000
Yahiko's in trouble?

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:40.840
Yeah. Okay, got it.

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:41.760
Hold on.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:46.510
Abeno-san, Zenko wants 
us to come to the temple.

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:49.510
We'll be right there.

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:54.110
Did Yahiko cause more trouble for Zenko?

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:57.270
That's not what it sounded like.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:01.360
<i>The weather was fair 
across the country today,</i>

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:06.660
<i>but clouds will gradually spread 
as the night wears on...</i>

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:15.230
You're those boys from the other day!

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:16.420
<i>Zenko's father!</i>

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:19.990
They're here.

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:37.690
Thank you.

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:40.950
I had fun.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:44.020
I had a fantastic time.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:48.020
There is no happiness like this.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.830
Thank you.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.460
Thank you...

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time "The Fool"</b>

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:29.340
Abeno-san, I learned how to write the 
"itsuki" in "Haruitsuki" without looking!

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:30.010
So what?

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:31.240
Isn't that amazing?

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:32.930
Not even the Mononokean can do it!

00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:37.060
Then next, write the characters for "rose," 
"melancholy," "giraffe," and "skull."

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:38.080
Without looking, of course.

00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:39.690
What? Why?!
